From: WGpuFury <wgpufury@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:39:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add WGPUInstanceFlag_D3D12DRED: say what the GPU was doing
 when it was removed

With the flag (or WithEnv and WGPU_D3D12_DRED=1), wgpu-native turns on
Direct3D 12 Device Removed Extended Data before devices are created:
auto-breadcrumbs with their PIX event and marker names, and page-fault
tracking. When a device is removed, the device-lost message then names
each command list the GPU didn't finish, the operation it stopped at, the
debug groups around it, and a page-fault address with the allocations
there. d3d12.dll is loaded at run time, as wgpu-hal does.
